{
  "dom_id": "step-e5433",
  "name": "Example: Determining a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix",
  "problem": "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is $[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]$",
  "worked_solution": "Consider a general vector $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8x-y \\\\ -5x-2y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
